---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { checkerUrl, sitePath } from '../../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  article
  title="Instagram relationship guides: prepare, compare & interpret"
  description="Practical MutualLens guides for preparing an Instagram export, fixing file problems, understanding relationship terms, and reading saved snapshots."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">MUTUALLENS GUIDES</p><h1>
    Prepare the files.<br />Read the result carefully.
  </h1><p class="lede">
    Start with the task in front of you. These guides explain what the local
    checker accepts, how its relationship groups are calculated, and where the
    evidence stops.
  </p>
  <div class="guide-index" aria-label="MutualLens guides">
    <a
      class="guide-card"
      href={sitePath('/guides/download-instagram-followers/')}
    >
      <span>EXPORT PREPARATION</span><h2>Prepare your relationship files</h2><p>
        Use official export controls, keep both directions and include every
        available split part.
      </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
    <a
      class="guide-card"
      href={sitePath('/guides/instagram-export-troubleshooting/')}
    >
      <span>TROUBLESHOOTING</span><h2>Resolve missing or unclear files</h2><p>
        Work through missing directions, ambiguous loose files, nested ZIPs,
        unsupported archives and qualified results.
      </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
    <a class="guide-card" href={sitePath('/guides/followers-vs-following/')}>
      <span>TERMINOLOGY</span><h2>Followers, following and mutuals</h2><p>
        See how two fictional lists become three relationship groups, without
        turning a difference into a judgment.
      </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
    <a class="guide-card" href={sitePath('/guides/reading-snapshot-history/')}>
      <span>SNAPSHOTS</span><h2>Read changes between saved reports</h2><p>
        Learn which dates and account labels make snapshots compatible, and what
        an observed change can and cannot prove.
      </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
    <a
      class="guide-card"
      href={sitePath('/guides/not-following-back-vs-unfollowed/')}
    >
      <span>INTERPRETATION</span><h2>Separate a result from an unfollow</h2><p>
        “Not following back” describes one comparison. “Unfollowed” requires
        compatible observations over time.
      </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </div>
  <aside class="article-note">
    <strong>Automatic checking remains unavailable.</strong><p>
      These guides describe the working local-import preview. They do not claim
      that a website-only live scan has passed its completeness, scale or
      recurring free-capacity gates.
    </p>
  </aside>
  <div class="article-actions">
    <a class="button primary" href={checkerUrl('import')}
      >Open upload mode <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    ><a href={sitePath('/')}>Return to the checker overview</a>
  </div>
</Page>
